adr: 0363
file: lib/dialect/paserror.pas
kills: lib_boundary_nul
why: HoldsNul answers false for everything, so every one of the nineteen guards lets a name holding chr(0) through to ADR-0122's crossing and the first of them stops the program. The case prints one line per routine and the golden has nineteen; a stop at the first leaves none.
--- old
  HoldsNul := false;
  for k := 1 to length(s) do
    if s[k] = chr(0) then exit(true)
--- new
  HoldsNul := false;
  for k := 1 to 0 do
    if s[k] = chr(0) then exit(true)
